# ROVEXO Implementation Protection Law v1.1 (ABSOLUTE P0 · LEVEL 8 · LOCKED)

## Mission

Owner-approved = Canonical Implementation · Protected · One SSOT · One version · Protected architecture, design, and logic — **as a whole**.

Integrity includes: Design · UI · UX · Components · Layout · Navigation · Responsive/Adaptive · Business/Financial logic · APIs · States · Performance · A11y · Browser · Architecture · Scalability.

## Forbidden after approval

Redesign · recreate · duplicate · replace · split · migrate · hidden/experimental/temporary versions · duplicated systems / business logic / layouts / engines / implementations

## Allowed (must stay functionally + visually identical)

Bug · performance · a11y · responsive/adaptive · security · browser · infrastructure · API · database · optimization in place

## No Regression Law

Never: reduce functionality/a11y/responsiveness/performance · introduce regressions · break approved flows/components/integrations/navigation/layouts.  
**Better or identical. Never worse.**

## Five Absolute Questions (order)

1. Root cause? **No → STOP**  
2. Fix root cause without changing Owner-approved implementation? **Yes → fix only that**  
3. Can existing be optimized? **Yes → optimize**  
4. New implementation absolutely required? **No → forbidden**  
5. Without v2 / duplicated systems/engines/layouts/components/logic? **Yes → proceed · No → Owner approval**

## Principles

**Four golden:** One implementation · Owner-approved always wins · Optimize before rebuild · Simplify before expand  

**Five absolute:** Protect before modify · Code last · No regression · 100/100 only · The implementation always wins  

**If no root cause → do not touch it. If not 100/100 → do not deploy.**

## Master equation

PROTECT + OPTIMIZE + PRESERVE + SIMPLIFY + ONE IMPLEMENTATION + ONE SSOT + ZERO REGRESSIONS + ZERO DUPLICATIONS + OWNER APPROVED DESIGN + MAXIMUM SCALABILITY = **ROVEXO**

